-- title:
--   Hasse principle for p-primary S-unit classes H²_S(Γ_L, E_S)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $S$ a finite set of rational primes with $p \in S$. Let $L$ be a finite intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure} \mathbb{Q}$ which is unramified outside $S$, in the sense that $L/\mathbb{Q}$ is finite and for every prime $q \notin S$ and every valuation subring $A$ of the algebraic closure with $q \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$ the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the fixing subgroup $\Gamma_L$ of $L$. Let $a$ be a class in `continuousH2Sr` for the inclusion $\Gamma_L \hookrightarrow \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, the set $S$ and the coefficient module `sUnitsMaxRep S L` (the $\mathbb{Z}$-representation of $\Gamma_L$ on the submodule `sUnitsMaxSubmodule S L` of $\operatorname{Additive}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})^\times$ cut out by `sUnitsMaxStable S L`); thus $a$ is a level-$S$ $2$-cocycle modulo the level-$S$ coboundaries. Assume $a$ is $p$-primary torsion, that is $p^k \cdot a = 0$ for some power of $p$ in $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume further that the image of $a$ in `continuousH2` restricts to zero at every finite place of $S$: for each $q \in S$ and each $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, the map `continuousH2Map` along the group homomorphism $h \mapsto \sigma\,\iota_q(h)\,\sigma^{-1}$ from the subgroup of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q)$ of those $h$ with $\sigma\,\iota_q(h)\,\sigma^{-1} \in \Gamma_L$ into $\Gamma_L$ (here $\iota_q$ is `primeLocalToGlobal`), with the identity coefficient map into the restricted representation, sends `continuousH2SrToContinuousH2` applied to $a$ to zero; and, if $p = 2$, that the same holds with $\iota_q$ replaced by the inclusion of the subgroup generated by complex conjugation. Then $a = 0$.
--
--   This is the Hasse principle, that is the injectivity of the localisation map, for the $p$-primary part of $H^2(G_{L,S}, E_S)$, the $S$-integral Brauer group of $L$, with local conditions imposed through the genuine restriction maps to the decomposition subgroups at the places of $S$ and at the archimedean place, and with coefficients kept in the $S$-units of the maximal extension unramified outside $S$. Unlike the companion form of the statement, no hypothesis that $\sqrt{-1} \in L$ is made when $p = 2$; instead the archimedean local condition is assumed. It is used in the vanishing statement for level-$S$ classes of the Galois $S$-unit representation obtained by restriction to $L(\sqrt{-1})$.
